  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "The general solution of the differential equation $\\frac{d y}{d x}+\\sin (x+y)=\\sin (x-y)$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "FnGP4",
      "text": "$\\log \\tan y+\\sin x=\\mathrm{C}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "mjK8K",
      "text": "$\\quad \\log \\tan \\frac{y}{2}+2 \\sin x=\\mathrm{C}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "aUd2m",
      "text": "$\\tan \\frac{y}{2}+\\log \\sin x=\\mathrm{C}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "wZvg4",
      "text": "None of these",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "The equation is,\r\n\r\n$\\frac{d y}{d x}=\\sin (x-y)-\\sin (x+y)=2 \\cos x \\sin (-y)$\r\n\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\frac{d y}{\\sin y}+2 \\cos x d x=0$\r\n\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\int \\cos e c y d y+2 \\int \\cos x d x=\\mathrm{C}$\r\n\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\log \\tan \\frac{y}{2}+2 \\sin x=\\mathrm{C}$",
    "image": null
  },
